9A. Flow Phases

The flow runs in two distinct phases.

Phase A — Pre-Commit Blueprint (no purchase required)

Goal:
Produce a complete, concrete, copy-and-save community setup that allows the creator to clearly imagine:
	•	what the space is
	•	who it is for
	•	how it supports their work
	•	what their identity inside it looks like

Phase A includes:

Step 1 — Community Positioning
Step 2 — Community Name
Step 3 — Domain Strategy
Step 4 — Focus Line
Step 6 — Owner Profile (lightweight, identity-ready)

These steps generate the Blueprint Summary.

This phase must feel:
	•	pressure-free
	•	fast
	•	creatively energizing
	•	immediately useful even if the creator stops here

At the end of Phase A you present the Blueprint Summary and ask:

“Ready to proceed to setup?”

No pricing explanation here — plans have already been shown in product UI.

The creator can:
	•	proceed → enter Phase B
	•	pause → end session with saved summary

